<component type="desktop-application">
  <id>org.docking.Docking</id>
  <name>Docking</name>
  <summary>Customizable X11 dock with previews, applets, and rich drag and drop</summary>
  <metadata_license>CC0-1.0</metadata_license>
  <project_license>GPL-3.0-or-later</project_license>
  <developer_name>Eduardo Mucelli Rezende Oliveira</developer_name>
  <launchable type="desktop-id">org.docking.Docking.desktop</launchable>
  <description>
    <p>
      Docking is a lightweight but feature-rich dock for Linux desktop environments
      built with Python, GTK 3, and Cairo. It focuses on fast launcher workflows,
      polished hover behavior, and a practical applet system while staying close to
      the simplicity that makes docks useful in day-to-day desktop work.
    </p>
    <p>
      It supports pinned launchers, running-window indicators, window previews,
      autohide, drag and drop, folders and files in the dock, theme selection,
      geometry-aware hover behavior, and a growing built-in applet catalog.
      Current runtime support targets X11 desktop sessions.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Pin launchers, files, folders, and separators directly in the dock</li>
      <li>Use hover previews, tooltips, and rich app menus for open windows</li>
      <li>Customize themes, position, icon behavior, and autohide timing</li>
      <li>Enable built-in applets such as clock, weather, battery, clipboard, and network</li>
    </ul>
  </description>
